lly shows a low  plasma blood glucose plasma cortisol  measured between 8:00 a.m. and 9:00 a.m.  show a value of less than 3 milligrams  per deciliter ACTH stimulation test is  important tests to diagnose Addison's  disease in which we give 250 milligrams  of exogenous ACTH to the patient in a  normal case the plasma cortisol should  rise above 19 milligrams per deciliter  but in Addison's disease the plasma  cutter soul does not rise above 90  milligrams per deciliter plasma is ETH  levels are usually elevated above 100  picograms per deciliter due to the  reflux increase in the ACTH levels in  cases of autoimmune original itis organ  specific antibodies can be detected in  the plasma of the patients like adrenal  cortex antibodies and 21 hydroxylase  antibodies the patients of Addison's  disease usually have anemia and Osuna  failure treatment of Addison's disease  usually depends upon the hormonal  replacement cortisol is replaced by  prednisone and those of five milligrams  in the morning and two point five  milligrams in the evening aldosterone is  replaced by fludrocortisone which is  given in a dose range of 0.05 to  point one milligrams per day and this  treatment usually runs lifelong one  quick mention I would like to do here is  the adrenal crisis which is certain  severe adrenal insufficiency occurring  in cases of stress infection it is a  life-threatening condition and requires  emergency management in the form of  intravenous injections of  glucocorticoids and also large volumes  of intravenous dextrose normal saline  solution so this was a brief overview  about the Addison's disease thank you so  much for watching this video make sure  to subscribe us on YouTube for all the  latest videos and also make sure to  follow us on Facebook for the latest  updates
 

